INFO 8508 :: Page 30 :: 345 PM Balto Jany 6th 1865 Balto 3 PM for QMGenl . The Captain of the Steamer Baltic reports his vessel at Swann point twenty miles below this City and that she cannot come nearer with safety . he requires an anchor and chain and seven hundred and fifty tons of coal it will take five days at least to Coal the vessel at Annapolis and get the anchor from NY she can go to N York coal get her anchor and return to Annapolis sooner than chain she can be got ready at the latter point . Shall I order her to NY for these purposes ? I ordered her anchor yesterday morning but can stop the ship - ment and have it put a board at New York . The Ariel , Victor , and Illinois are here coaling RM Newport Col & chf qm 620 PM Ft Monroe Jan 6 . 1865 <deletion>330 PM</deletion> Dated 1.30 PM Mrs Ellen H. Stanton Washn ---- arrived here safely will remain until tomorrow morning & then start for Savannah Edwin M Stanton
INFO 7681 :: Page 23 :: 345 PM 3 PM City Pt Jany 3rd 65 Gen Halleck Special orders 298 and 299 have not been received here U. S. Grant Lt Genl 5 P. M. Fortress Monroe Va Jan 3. 1865 430 P. M. for Br Gen Ingalls ---- I have ordered the Steamers CC Leary, Ariel, & Victor to report to Col Newport Balto. ---- By direction Chf Qr Mr Sigd Wm L. James Capt. a Q M another to Capt E. L Allen - in complying with the request of Gen Ingalls I have consumed all surplus transportation ---- By direction Chf Q. M. Signed ---- Wm L James Capt a qm 5.30 P. M N. Y. Jan 3. 1865. N. Y. 3rd for Qr. Mr. Genl. Washn. can also obtain the Surro - nada 12 00 men & 16 ft loaded ---- she is coaled & can start in 24 hours hours ---- Another steamer the Oriental is expected tomorrow morning ---- she can carry one thousand men ---- does the Ericsson draw too much water ---- she is being got ready Q. M. S. Van Vliet. Br. Gen and Q. M.
INFO 8511 :: Page 33 :: 12.40 P. M Winchester Jany 7th 1865 To Secy of War The Transports were not ready at Baltimore for Genl Grover and he had to go in to camp this is unfortunate PH Sheridan Maj Genl 730 P. M. Balto Jan 7. 1865. 6 PM for QrMrGen Your dispatch rec'd neither the Surro Nada , Ashland or Oriental have arrived here & I know nothing of their capacity --- The Ariel , Illinois , Victor & Genl Sedgwick now here can carry three thousand men & one hundred horses ---- transportation is required for five thousand soldiers two hundred & thirty horses & for one thousand men of the Construction Corps Expected from the west ---- the Baltic left for Ft. Monroe last night Sig R. M. Newport Col. & Q. M. 9.20 A. M. Jan 8. 1865 Ft. Monroe Va Jan 7. 1865 8 P. M. for Sec Navy ---- The main Journal in 12 hours run shows new cracks , some of them serious . Chf Engineer Robie & Mr Cosgrove contractors Engineer think that from the edges of these cracks reaming away the brass bearings , there will be danger of a break down in going to Wilmington Jno Rodgers
